From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:14:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 33/75] Set addition: give equal set types the lower base of
 the two so constant range checks see the real type

---
 compiler/nadd.pas | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/nadd.pas b/compiler/nadd.pas
index 3d06eb22..8ed47109 100644
--- a/compiler/nadd.pas
+++ b/compiler/nadd.pas
@@ -3042,7 +3042,17 @@ const
                     else
                        inserttypeconv(right,tsetdef(nd).elementdef);
                   end;
-              end;
+              end
+             { Set types with the same element type, base, size and upper
+               bound are equal even if their lower bounds differ. The result
+               gets the type of the left operand, so if the right one starts
+               lower, give the left one the right's type, else the result type
+               does not cover all of its elements (a later range check of a
+               constant set would then fail for a valid element). This only
+               changes the type, the representation is the same. }
+             else if (rd.typ=setdef) and
+                     (tsetdef(rd).setlow<tsetdef(ld).setlow) then
+               inserttypeconv(left,rd);
           end
          { pointer comparison and subtraction }
          else if (
